00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:12.257
The wildly recognized phenomenon is that
organizations are on a pretty

00:00:12.257 --> 00:00:16.939
regular basis, walking back on the
promises they made to their employees.

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:21.398
So they cut pension benefits, retiree,
healthcare.

00:00:21.398 --> 00:00:27.155
Oftentimes, people come in to places being
promised things that and those implicit

00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:32.601
psychological contracts are broken and
that's not really news in some sense.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:37.801
On the other hand, there is this idea of a
very powerful and longstanding

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:42.842
social theory, social idea, which talks
about the norm of reciprocity.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:47.626
That when you do something for someone,
particularly if you do something nice for

00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:50.899
someone, that, that person ought to repay
the favor.

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:53.893
So, if I give you a ride, you ought to
give me a ride.

00:00:53.893 --> 00:00:57.282
If I invite you over for dinner, you
should invite me over for

00:00:57.282 --> 00:00:59.014
dinner, things such as that.

00:00:59.014 --> 00:01:01.840
And so you have on the one hand this
wonderful,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.553
this continuity between organizations that
seem to be breaking promises and

00:01:06.553 --> 00:01:11.118
breaking their, their, you know, not
really rewarding the hard work and

00:01:11.118 --> 00:01:13.896
good efforts of their employees that put
in.

00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:16.138
On, on the other hand, there's no
reciprocity.

00:01:16.138 --> 00:01:18.603
[MUSIC]

00:01:18.603 --> 00:01:22.210
The intuition that we had is that as soon
as you put people into

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:27.165
an organizational context, you told them
as opposed to a personal relationship,

00:01:27.165 --> 00:01:29.099
they were now an organization.

00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:31.939
Instead of a favor being done for them by
a friend,

00:01:31.939 --> 00:01:35.065
it was being done by a coworker and things
such as that.

00:01:35.065 --> 00:01:39.635
But that would change the dynamic in some
fundamental ways that would cause

00:01:39.635 --> 00:01:44.276
the favor, the person who receives the
favor to feel less obligated to repay

00:01:44.276 --> 00:01:48.991
the favor simply, because it was delivered
in an organizational setting and

00:01:48.991 --> 00:01:51.265
that's essentially what we found.

00:01:51.265 --> 00:01:54.625
Now there's some mechanisms that underly
this, one mechanism,

00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:56.367
if you think about a reciprocity.

00:01:56.367 --> 00:02:00.093
Means if you've done me a favor in the
past, I should,

00:02:00.093 --> 00:02:03.902
following the normal reciprocity, repay
that favor.

00:02:03.902 --> 00:02:09.546
However, organizations are not about the
past, they're about the future.

00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:10.794
And so therefore,

00:02:10.794 --> 00:02:15.326
to the extent that you are not gonna be
useful to me in the future.

00:02:15.326 --> 00:02:19.886
Or not gonna be helpful to me in my job or
career, then I won't feel as

00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:24.533
obligated to repay the favor in a in an
organizational setting.

00:02:24.533 --> 00:02:28.771
Because organizations are, are very much
about thinking about the future.

00:02:28.771 --> 00:02:33.327
Organizations also prompt a more
calculative or strategic mindset where

00:02:33.327 --> 00:02:37.303
you're always thinking about is can
somebody be useful or not.

00:02:37.303 --> 00:02:38.789
Can they be helpful or not.

00:02:38.789 --> 00:02:43.838
And so when you get a favor done for you
in an organizational setting, you're less

00:02:43.838 --> 00:02:48.982
likely to attribute that kindness to some
trait or disposition of the individual.

00:02:48.982 --> 00:02:52.605
And more likely to attribute it the fact,
well, they were just doing their job.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.432
And that also then diminishes the
pressures or

00:02:55.432 --> 00:02:58.847
the the likelihood that you will repay
that favor.

00:02:58.847 --> 00:03:02.108
Because it's not really a favor, it was
just part of their job.

00:03:02.108 --> 00:03:11.844
[MUSIC]

